A||N||5||LMFIERO||No heat and temp gauge. =(||||1||
Z||000000||LMFIERO||11-28-2001||01:57 AM||||Recently my Heater Core went and the AC belt was lose and had worn a hole into the lower RAD to engine hose.<BR>I have replaced the heater core. And the Lower RAD HOSE to Engine, along with the thermostat. Then took it in to have the cooling system professionally drained cleaned and filled.<BR>I have no heat. Being winter it would be nice.<BR>My temp gauge in the car also stopped working.<BR>I am baffled as to what it could be. I felt the line coming into the heater core and it is hot as......rhymes with well.<BR>Still no heat and no gauge.<P>CAN any one help please.||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||11-28-2001||03:12 AM||||You don't say if you have a 2.5L 4-cyl or a 2.8L V-6 but I am assuming that it is the 2.8 -- the temperature sensor for the gauge is located just to the left side of the rear head right above the manifold (next to the coil) - there you will see two wires - one wire is for the water temp light and one wire is for the gauge itself - check and see if it has been unplugged or damaged (due to the proximity to the manifold they become brittle and break out leaving just the wires connected to the sensor) --<P>You also don't say whether the heater blower is blowing air but just not <I>hot</I> air ... if the blower is working you may have a defective heat select cable (runs from the bottom of the heater and a/c control above the radio, under the dash on the passenger side and up to the heat duct - this opens the heater door when put in the heat position -- move the selector lever to different positions and listen for the heat door to open and close - if you do not hear it the chances are that the select cable had become disconnected under the dash...... you can remove the right speaker from the dash and see the cable on the top of the heat duct........<P>Hope this helps.......<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-28-2001||06:50 AM||||also if they didnt follow the correct way to fill radiator, you could have an airlock in the heater core.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||11-28-2001||07:49 AM||||Is your radiator fan hot wired to the ignition switch?<BR>If it is it will take forever to warm up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||LMFIERO||11-29-2001||12:25 AM||||Just thanking everyone for their ideas. I have fixed the heating problem. It turns out that one of the hoses going into the heater core was kinked. We un-kinked the hose and BAM............. I had heat.<P>The guage still does not work. It will flicker on when I turn the car on then it will go back to the starting position. It will not rise as the car heats up. I think the sensor is gone. Any ideas?<P>Ohh ya the car is a 1986 SE V6 2.8 litre.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||11-29-2001||07:37 AM||||As stated above, just try grounding both wires going to the temp sender. If the gauge pegs and the idiot light comes on(key on of course) then a bad sender is a good bet.||||reg||1
